# Docs — etude-3xt

Three docs files changed. Every long-lived docs path was checked; the no-change
decisions and their reasons are below, path by path.

## Docs debt this phase owed

From the plan, implement and verify gates, four items plus one wording fix:

| Owed | Where it landed |
|---|---|
| the `retro markdown <path>` stdout line — **the string that actually ships**, not the plan's `wrote <path>` | `docs/retro.md` capture Output block + generate Output block |
| the `retro_file` manifest key, and that it is **not always** `<retro-id>.md` | `docs/retro.md` §"The landed markdown" + §"Provenance" |
| capture does **not** `git add` the landed file | `docs/retro.md` §"The landed markdown", first bullet |
| non-zero exit **after** a successful ref commit if the file write fails | `docs/retro.md` §"The landed markdown", third bullet |
| create-only: an existing file is an error, never an overwrite | same section, second bullet (not owed, but it is user-visible and belongs with the other two) |

The plan's contract table said `wrote <path>`; the code ships
`retro markdown <path>`, because nothing is written in the in-place case. The
docs describe the shipped string. This artifact is the record that the drift was
deliberate.

## Files changed

### `docs/retro.md` — canonical product docs (the Retro guide in `mkdocs.yml` nav)

1. **Capture output block** — replaced the one-line "Prints `captured …` and
   `ref …`" with the actual three-line block including
   `retro markdown .etude/retros/<retro-id>.md`.
2. **New §"The landed markdown"** — the substantive addition. States why the
   landing exists (one command produces both artifacts, so neither can appear
   without the other), the two cases (outside the dir → land under the retro id;
   already inside → recorded in place, nothing written), and the consequence that
   `retro_file` is not always `<retro-id>.md` — *"A consumer that needs the
   correspondence must read `refs.retro_file` out of each manifest; deriving the
   filename from the ref id reports a false gap on every in-place capture."*
   Then the three behaviors above: not staged, create-only, non-zero exit after
   a successful ref write with the literal error text.
3. **Generate §"Output"** — added the third line, plus that a generated body has
   no source path so it always lands under the allocated id, with a link to the
   new section.
4. **Generate §"Provenance"** — added `retro_file` to the `metadata:` example and
   noted that all three derived keys (`produced_via`, `generator`, `retro_file`)
   are rejected as `--ref` values, quoting the message that ships
   (`is reserved; etude sets it`).

### `docs/plans/dogfood/retro-ledger.md` — the practice doc lanes follow

Added a paragraph to §"Retro cadence": **"Run capture, don't hand-write the
markdown."** This is the doc change that actually addresses the bead's practice
half. It gives the sequence (draft → `etude retro capture` → `git add` the
printed path → commit → push branch and refs), names the failure it prevents
(three retro files on epic `etude-9uf`, two refs, a cadence check counting the
refs), says what to do if you already wrote the file (pass that path to
`--file`), and states plainly that **nothing yet detects a hand-written retro
with no ref — that is bead `etude-24d`.**

That last sentence is deliberate. This doc claims a capability ("capture and the
markdown cannot diverge") and would be misread as claiming the whole symptom is
fixed; naming the surviving gap and its bead is the honest form.

### `docs/plans/dogfood/retro-capture.md` — the retro-capture planning note

Three sentences near the top: capture lands the markdown and records
`refs.retro_file`, an in-place body is recorded rather than copied, the file is
not staged, pointer to `docs/retro.md`. This file is the first thing a reader
lands on for "how are retros captured here", so it would have been stale
immediately.

